   "flags": {},
   "order": 12,
   "mode": 0,
   "inputs": [],
   "outputs": [],
   "properties": {},
   "widgets_values": [
    "## starter 07 \u00b7 3d model to regions\n\n**You need:** Blender 4.x installed (it runs in the background). No AI models.\n\n**Your own model:** paste the path of your .blend / .fbx / .obj / .abc / .glb / .usd into `file` of **scene render** (Explorer: right click the file, Copy as path). Empty = the sample building.\n\n**Do:** Queue. The sample building (a 24 x 16 m facade, every stone a part of its own) is rendered from the projector\n(30 m from the wall, 1.5 m up, the picture fitted to the model by lens shift). Scene render gives clay, depth\nand ID passes; every window, column and cornice becomes a region, tagged left / centre / right and by floor. The plan\ngives them prompts, scene measure the real size of a pixel on the wall, and the previz shows the picture on the\nbuilding from two audience spots.\n\n**Camera of your own model:** a file with a projection camera: unplug the projector node and set width / height\nto 0, then the file's camera and render size are used. A file without one: keep the projector and put your\nprojector's resolution into width / height.\n\n**Then try:** `throw_ratio` 1.2 on the projector (a real lens: the report says how much of the model the picture\ncovers); `aim = tilt`; `preview_pass = parts`; connect the plan to a **region sampler** as in starter 02\n(image = clay) to paint the facade.\n"
   ],
   "title": "read me"
  }
